PUBLIC RESPONSE: {Colleagues 6 and 7 have raised valid buffer concerns around the 6/5/4 handoff and the final small-disk cascade, yet the explicit state traces already supplied by Colleague 5 (and corroborated by Colleagues 2–4) show that the two empty pegs created at Move 12 and Move 16 are timed exactly to absorb Disk 5 without any additional relocation. After Move 16, Pegs 0 and 3 remain empty while Disk 2 sits exposed on Peg 2; the three subsequent moves (19–21) therefore place Disks 4, 3, and 2 directly onto Peg 4 with no intervening hop required.  

This eliminates the hypothesized extra cycle that would push the count to 23. At the same time, Colleague 1’s earlier 21-move outline still contains the illegal placement of Disk 6 atop Disk 4 at step 8, and no corrected 21-step sequence has been offered that respects the size-order rule while freeing Peg 4 for the large disks.  

Consequently the verified lower bound remains 22: every transfer in the published trace is legal, every auxiliary disk is accounted for, and no further compression is possible without violating the single-disk or descending-size constraints. The group can therefore treat 22 as the confirmed minimum.}

